---
title: Chinese Clear Stock
description: A meat stock that forms the basis of many Chinese recipes
source: The Chinese Kitchen <urn:isbn:9781856267021>
author: Deh-Ta Hsiung
yield: 4%litres
locale: en_GB
prep time: 20m
cook time: 4h30m
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Chinese
tags:
- meat
- poultry
- savoury
- ingredient
- chinese
---

Trim and discard excess fat from the @chicken{1%kg} and @pork spare ribs{1%kg}. Place the meat in a #large pot{}. Add about @cold water{6%litres}. Bring to a rapid boil over high heat and skim off the scum.

Add the @spring onions{6}(white parts only), @fresh ginger{50%g}(crushed), and @rice wine{4%tbsp}. Reduce the heat and simmer gently, covered, for 3.5 to ~{4%hours}.

Remove and discard all the solid ingredients, then strain the stock.

> If refrigerated when cool, the stock will keep for up to 4-5 days. Alternatively, it can be frozen in small quantities and defrosted as required.